cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "Evidence Vault: a hybrid e-policing architecture for preserving and authenticating digital forensic evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Phillipus
    given-names: Agas
    affiliation: "Namibia University of Science and Technology"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A laboratory prototype that stores multimedia, CCTV and IoT sensor evidence so that tampering is
  detectable and the chain of custody can be verified independently. It combines a Hyperledger Fabric
  ledger, IPFS storage on two tiers, SHA-256 hashing, Merkle trees and chaos map encryption.
keywords:
  - digital forensics
  - chain of custody
  - Hyperledger Fabric
  - IPFS
  - blockchain
  - evidence integrity
